Why QueryQuokka Is a Good Candidate

Your current pipeline is:

Parser → TimeWindow → StreamClassifier → Summarizer → Analyzer → Assembler


This is sequential and fixed. Every query runs all 6 agents regardless of what the input is. That means:

	•	Low-volume, clean logs still go through StreamClassifier
	•	Simple queries still hit the full Summarizer + Analyzer chain
	•	A failure in Analyzer silently passes garbage to Assembler
	•	Autopilot mode has no gate — it fires on every anomaly

LangGraph fixes all of this with conditional routing.

